Flynn is an autonomous software agent whose runs are governed and recorded.

Usage:
  flynn [flags] <command> [args]
  flynn [flags]

With no command, flynn starts an interactive session in a terminal.

Start and drive work:
  goal          Drive an objective to completion in the current directory
  resume        Continue a parked or interrupted run
  steer         Redirect a run that is still going
  kill          Stop a run that is still going
  watch         Run each ai! or ai? comment in the working tree as a turn
  review        Review a pull request and submit a verdict

Inspect runs and the record:
  runs          List past runs with their id, phase and objective
  inspect       Replay a past run's recorded events
  status        Show the live overview, or one run's phase and progress
  ps            List instances with their live, heartbeat-aware state
  get           List the resources of a kind
  describe      Show one resource's fields and recent change history
  diff          Show the fields that differ between two resources
  spine         Verify or export a run's signed record

Models:
  models        Browse the model catalog and manage local models
  init          Set up a model on this machine and make it the default

Integrations and extensions:
  auth          Store and manage API keys and integration credentials
  integrations  List integrations, show one, or call an operation
  extensions    Link, list, call or remove a local extension
  deps          List and install the external tools integrations need
  playbook      List the playbooks or run one
  mcp           Serve the toolset to an MCP client over stdio

Memory and skills:
  memory        Review, promote and forget what this install remembers
  skill         List and show skills, or measure whether one helps
  regrade       Re-grade learned skills against the working directory

Run as a service:
  serve         Answer chat messages and expose the monitor API
  deploy        Deploy through a hosting extension and track the service
  services      List or remove the managed services

Maintenance:
  version       Print the running build, or list the releases
  upgrade       Replace this binary with a newer verified release
  notices       Show the security advisories and notices for this build
  db            Print, back up or reset the state database
  sandbox       Check whether this host allows the sandbox
  help          Show help for flynn, a command or the flags

Global flags:
  --model <provider:model>  model as provider:model (default
                            "anthropic:claude-opus-5-5")
  --data-dir <string>       directory for the durable state database
  -v, --verbose             show tool arguments, outputs and per-turn detail
  --version                 print the version and exit
  -h, --help                show help for flynn or for a command

Run 'flynn help <command>' for a command's usage, flags and examples.
Run 'flynn help flags' for every flag, and 'flynn help goal' for goal specs.
